  "title": "What If One Driver Did Every Uber Trip?",
  "description": "Uber did 4.1 billion rides and deliveries last quarter. Now picture one driver.\n\nSources:\n- Uber: Uber Announces Results for Third Quarter 2026: https://investor.uber.com/news-events/news/press-release-details/2026/Uber-Announces-Results-for-Third-Quarter-2026/default.aspx\n\nUber Q3 2026 (Nov 4 2026): 4.1 billion trips in the quarter, up 16%. Trips = Mobility rides plus Delivery orders. Uber: more than 83 billion trips since 2010. Our math: 4.1 billion / 92 days = about 44.6 million a day, about 516 a second; one trip a minute = about 85 years for one day's trips; 83 billion trips at one a minute = about 158,000 years. Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #uber #whatif #howtheymakemoney",
